# Canon in D, duet (repertoire plan: canon-in-d). Your part is Pachelbel's two-bar ground bass,
# one note per beat, on the frets the plan gives: D (open string 4), A (open 5), B (string 5
# fret 2), F# (string 6 fret 2), G (string 6 fret 3), D, G, A; first position, finger = fret.
# Then the same eight bars again with you on chords, one downstrum per beat: D, A, the open Bm7
# (x20202, the easier shape before barre chords), the small F#m (xx4222, finger 1 across strings
# 3 to 1 at fret 2), G, D, G, A. Chord names (and diagrams) appear only there, where you strum
# them; in the first half the harmony is the same, D A Bm F#m G D G A, with your notes as roots.
# The app plays the canon above, as the original opens: three violins enter two bars apart, each
# with the same line (first in quarters, then quarters again, then eighths), read an octave lower
# for guitar. Only this opening of the canon is used. The violins' landing note in bar 9 and the
# closing D chord in bar 17 are added for this arrangement.
title: Canon in D (duet)
id: canon-in-d
composer: Johann Pachelbel
source: Canon for three violins and continuo, c. 1680-1706 (first published 1919); the opening, arranged as a guitar duet for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Pachelbel died in 1706); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 4
tags: duet, ground bass, baroque, canon
tempo: 60
time: 4/4
key: D

